cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  tm-vocabulary: an event-dated USPTO trademark corpus and a lead/lag text
  measure for the commercial economy
message: >-
  If you use this software, the corpus build, or the published panels, please
  cite the paper below. Derived panels containing patent counts additionally
  require attribution to PatentsView (CC-BY-4.0); see DATA_SOURCES.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Silver
    given-names: Eric
    email: epsilver@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/ericsilver/tm-vocabulary
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Re-parses all 13.99 million USPTO trademark case files into event-dated
  prosecution histories and scores every filing on how surprising its
  goods/services language is against what its industry filed in the five years
  before and the five years after. Atypicality is the average of the two
  divergences; lead is their signed difference.
keywords:
  - trademarks
  - innovation measurement
  - text as data
  - Kullback-Leibler divergence
  - USPTO
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Vocabulary position and trademark lifecycles: an event-dated corpus and a
    lead/lag text measure for the commercial economy
  authors:
    - family-names: Silver
      given-names: Eric
  year: 2026
